    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "body": "### Problem\n\n`@lsp.type.formatSpecifier` is not defined by default in [highlight_group.c](https://github.com/neovim/neovim/blob/master/src/nvim/highlight_group.c), so it falls back to `@lsp`.\n\n### Expected behavior\n\nIt would be nicer if for example `@lsp.type.formatSpecifier` was linked to `@string.special` by default.\n\nIt would resemble how in C printf syntax %d are identified as `cFormat` which links to `Special`.",
    "closed_at": null,
    "closed_by": null,
    "comment_data": [
        {
            "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
            "body": "Hmm, looking around, this seems to be a semantic token introduced in rust-analyzer. Not sure if it's actually globally standard?\n\nSee: https://github.com/rust-lang/rust-analyzer/pull/4183\n\nSo not sure if it's good to put in global defaults or may be it should be up to color theme authors to handle. For now I'll add it to my theme at least.",
            "created_at": "2026-10-18T16:25:17Z",
